    "body": "Yeah, I think 10k iterations were a compromise to avoid having very long test times. The changes in the tests right now do not guarantee failure in those cases but are much more stronger since now we wait for all blocks to finish exactly once.\r\n\r\nHowever now the tests run a bit faster than before since we avoid sleeping too much, we can bump the number of iterations if you think it makes sense. What would be your accepted running time in an “average” machine?",
